Declare aspect_bazel_lib's toolchain repo rules reproducible so they can use the repo
contents cache.

These 16 repo rules either download an integrity-pinned binary or write a generated BUILD
file derived entirely from their own attributes, so both are reproducible. Without this,
15 `aspect_bazel_lib++toolchains+*` repos are refetched on every CI runner and miss the
remote repo contents cache.

This is a backport of the equivalent change in bazel-lib v3.2.1
(https://github.com/bazel-contrib/bazel-lib/pull/1267). v3 is published to the BCR under
the new module name `bazel_lib`, but `aspect_rules_ts` and `rules_oci` still depend on
`aspect_bazel_lib`, so adopting it would put both module trees in the graph rather than
replace this one. Drop this patch once those migrate.

diff -ruN '--exclude=e2e' bazel_lib.orig/lib/private/copy_directory_toolchain.bzl bazel_lib/lib/private/copy_directory_toolchain.bzl
--- a/lib/private/copy_directory_toolchain.bzl
+++ b/lib/private/copy_directory_toolchain.bzl
@@ -149,6 +149,12 @@
     # Base BUILD file for this repository
     rctx.file("BUILD.bazel", build_content)
 
+    # Bazel <8.3.0 lacks rctx.repo_metadata
+    if not hasattr(rctx, "repo_metadata"):
+        return None
+
+    return rctx.repo_metadata(reproducible = True)
+
 copy_directory_toolchains_repo = repository_rule(
     _copy_directory_toolchains_repo_impl,
     doc = """Creates a repository with toolchain definitions for all known platforms
@@ -185,6 +191,12 @@
     # Base BUILD file for this repository
     rctx.file("BUILD.bazel", build_content)
 
+    # Bazel <8.3.0 lacks rctx.repo_metadata
+    if not hasattr(rctx, "repo_metadata"):
+        return None
+
+    return rctx.repo_metadata(reproducible = True)
+
 copy_directory_platform_repo = repository_rule(
     implementation = _copy_directory_platform_repo_impl,
     doc = "Fetch external tools needed for copy_directory toolchain",
